Buildroot config to generate XRP hosted implementation where CPU cores
run host OS code and Xtensa DSP cores are connected to shared memory.

The Xtensa toolchain is expected to have the configs `D_233L_pif128_LC` and `visionp6_ao`.

Few environment variables must be set:

	export XTENSA_SYSTEM="/path/to/XtensaTools/config"
	export XTENSA_CORE="visionp6_ao"
	export PATH="${XTENSA_SYSTEM}/../bin:${PATH}"

To build:

	git clone https://github.com/foss-xtensa/buildroot.git
	git -C buildroot checkout xtensa-xrp

	mkdir buildroot-build
	make -C buildroot/ O=../buildroot-build/ xtsc_vp6_mp_xrp_defconfig
	make -C buildroot-build/

Find the kernel, root filesystem, etc ... under buildroot-build/images/

To run what was generated, we use `xtsc-run`.

We create the files needed by `xtsc-run`:

	mkdir subsystem
	cd subsystem
	cp ../buildroot/board/xtsc/vp6-mp/subsys.yml .
	${XTENSA_SYSTEM}/../libexec/xt-sysbuilder -subsys subsys.yml -swtools ${XTENSA_SYSTEM}/../ -build sysbuild
	ln -snf ../buildroot-build/images/rootfs.ext2 rootfs.ext2

We can now use `xtsc-run` to boot Linux:

	xtsc-run \
	--set_xtsc_parm=turbo=true \
	--define=Host_BINARY=../buildroot-build/images/Image.elf \
	--define=Host_BINARY_ARGS= \
	--define=DSP_0_BINARY= \
	--define=DSP_1_BINARY= \
	--include=sysbuild/xtsc-run/SubSystem.inc \
	--set_xtsc_parm="lua_script_files=sysbuild/xtsc-run/sim_cntrl.lua"

At the login prompt, enter `root`.

To run XRP hosted implementation, load the kernel module and start the userspace executable as follow:

	modprobe xrp_hw_simple
	xrp-host-hosted
